<title>USA: Baltimore Gas and Electric Co Q4 loss.</title>
<headline>Baltimore Gas and Electric Co Q4 loss.</headline>
<dateline>BALTIMORE 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Call consensus estimate for the fourth quarter was $0.23/shr. Company reported $0.33 -- including $0.10 from diversified businesses and $0.23 from utility -- before charge of $0.39 for settlement on replacemwent energy costs.</p>
<p>		   (In Thousands, Except Per Share Amounts)</p>
<p>				 Fourth Quarter	     Year</p>
<p>				1996	 1995	1996	 1995</p>
<p>Revenues</p>
<p> Electric	     $472,157   $503,554 $2,208,744 $2,229,774</p>
<p> Gas		     141,638    130,275    517,292    400,504</p>
<p>Diversified Businesses</p>
<p>			   120,455     91,883    427,211    304,521</p>
<p> Total		   734,250    725,712  3,153,247  2,934,799</p>
<p>Replacement Energy</p>
<p>  Costs	   ( 57,593)(a)	    -  ( 61,990)(b)	 -</p>
<p> Net Income	     ( 992)     52,929    310,824    338,007</p>
<p>Earnings Applicable to</p>
<p>  Common Stock	( 9,140)     42,486    272,288    297,429</p>
<p>Average Common Shares</p>
<p>  Outstanding	  147,620    147,527    147,560    147,527</p>
<p> Earnings Per Share   ( .06)	  .29	 1.85	 2.02</p>
<p>(a)  Charge that resulted from a settlement regarding</p>
<p>replacement energy costs associated with extended outages at BGE's Calvert Cliffs Nuclear Power Plant from 1989-1991.</p>
<p>(b)  Note (a) and the disallowance of $4.4 million after-tax ($0.03 per share) in replacement energy costs incurred during 1987 outages at Calvert Cliffs.</p>
<p>(c)  1995 year net includes the impact of the $0.07 per share write-off of construction work in progress costs after deciding to not construct the remainder of the first combined cycle generating unit at BGE's Perryman site.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
